help=**Events**\n`!event create` — guided event creation wizard\n`!event create | Title | YYYY-MM-DD H:mm | zone/default | limit/none | description/- | repeat | duration-minutes (optional) | notify-start yes/no (optional)`\n`!event list` — upcoming events\n`!event info ID` — details and attendees\n`!event rsvp ID yes|maybe|no` — change RSVP\n`!event cancel ID` — cancel your event\n`!event manage ID` — open host controls on demand\n`!event setup` — guided server setup (admins)\n`!event myzone Europe/Amsterdam` — time shown in private replies\n`!event zones` — time-zone examples\n`!event language` — language support and contribution info\n\n**Example**\n`!event create | Board Game Night | 2026-12-05 19:00 | default | 12 | Bring a game | weekly:4 | 120`\nUse the 24-hour clock. `default` uses the server zone. `1` or `none` means one event; `daily:2`, `weekly:4`, `monthly:3` means a series of 2–12 events. The optional last field is approximate duration in minutes (15–1440); omitted means the server default.\nStart setup in a server or DM me. Events are published only in the selected announcement channel. Leave duration empty to use the server default; append `yes` as the final field to DM the host and interested attendees when the event starts.
zones=**Time-zone examples**\nMoscow — `Europe/Moscow` · Kaliningrad — `Europe/Kaliningrad`\nYekaterinburg — `Asia/Yekaterinburg` · Novosibirsk — `Asia/Novosibirsk`\nVladivostok — `Asia/Vladivostok` · Minsk — `Europe/Minsk`\nAmsterdam — `Europe/Amsterdam` · Berlin — `Europe/Berlin`\nLondon — `Europe/London` · New York — `America/New_York` · Tokyo — `Asia/Tokyo`\n\nFull IANA zones and fixed offsets such as `UTC+2` or `GMT-5:30` are supported. Fixed offsets do not change for daylight saving time; use an IANA zone such as `Europe/Amsterdam` when seasonal clock changes should apply. `Europe` alone is not a time zone. Popular city aliases are supported too.
